description:
pkix-path-builder/src/lib.rs:933-935 (`build_first_valid_path` rustdoc, Errors section):

```
/// - [`Error::DepthExceeded`] / [`Error::BudgetExceeded`] — propagated from
///   [`build_path_candidates`] when the iterator surfaces them.
```

This is inaccurate. Tracing the implementation:

- The `PathCandidates::next` body (lib.rs:581-714) **never** yields `Error::DepthExceeded`. When `frames.len() > max_depth`, it silently backtracks (lib.rs:653-657) and the iterator returns `None` on exhaustion. The only fatal error the iterator surfaces is `BudgetExceeded` (lib.rs:619-622).
- `Error::DepthExceeded` is computed by the wrapper after the main iterator exhausts (lib.rs:1028-1043). The wrapper runs a fresh `PathCandidates` at `max_depth + 1`; if that probe yields any chain, the wrapper returns `Err(Error::DepthExceeded)`. This is "computed by the helper," not "propagated from the iterator."
- `BudgetExceeded` may come from either the main iterator OR the depth probe. The doc lumps both into "propagated from build_path_candidates" but the depth probe is a separate invocation.

A caller reading the doc and writing a recovery path assuming "DepthExceeded comes from the iterator and I can detect it before the wrapper retries with a larger budget" will be surprised: by the time `build_first_valid_path` returns `Err(Error::DepthExceeded)`, the depth probe already ran (one extra DFS budget worth of work that the caller didn't anticipate).

Suggested correction:

```
/// # Errors
///
/// - [`Error::NoPathFound`] — the underlying iterator yielded no candidates
///   and no candidates exist at any depth.
/// - [`Error::DepthExceeded`] — the underlying iterator yielded no candidates
///   within `max_depth`, but a depth-probe at `max_depth + 1` did. This
///   error is computed by this function, NOT yielded by the iterator
///   itself. The depth probe costs up to one additional `dfs_budget` of
///   DFS work.
/// - [`Error::BudgetExceeded`] — DFS frame-entry budget was exhausted,
///   either in the main candidate enumeration or in the post-exhaustion
///   depth probe.
/// - [`Error::NoValidPath`] — at least one candidate was yielded but none
///   passed `validate_path`. Carries `tried` (>= 1) and the last
///   `validate_path` error rendering.
```

Same correction applies to `build_path`'s rustdoc at lib.rs:771-779 — the existing wording there ("a path exists topologically but requires more than `max_depth` intermediates") is accurate behaviorally, but doesn't mention that detection costs an extra probe pass. Forward-link to the depth probe's hidden cost.

Minor — this is a doc-fidelity issue, not a behavior bug.
